{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540782-have-anyone-done-this","id":1540782,"title":"Have anyone done this?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-20T09:22:56-07:00","id":1540782,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Have anyone done this?","content":"Have anyone done a Mage the Ascension Technocracy Chronicle, where a Technocracy base ended up in the Chronicle of Darkness Earth? Now that magic doesn't run by the Consensus, Technocrat can still cast spell, but they can't raise their Arete more than 5, but recive Paradox from disbelief. And how would the Awaken mage interact with the Technocracy? This is using revised rule and lore by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T12:03:10-07:00","id":1540796,"title":"","content":"Why is it using Revised rules if they're in the CofD universe? Nonsense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T12:24:07-07:00","id":1540797,"title":"","content":"I believe the idea is that the Technocrats suddenly in the CofD-verse would be using the Mage the Ascension Revised Technocrat rules for how their magic works rather than them converting to Awakening mages in the process, rather than inherently using Revised WoD rules for everything.<br /> <br /> That, of course, makes the exercise kinda pointless because the CofD metaphysics don't allow for the Technocrats to do their Enlightened Science as they interpret it as it uses principles that don't exist in the CofD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T16:46:25-07:00","id":1540812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540782-have-anyone-done-this?p=1540797#post1540797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That, of course, makes the exercise kinda pointless because the CofD metaphysics don't allow for the Technocrats to do their Enlightened Science as they interpret it as it uses principles that don't exist in the CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that is necessary true, in Chronicle of Darkness Second Sight, Thaumaturge magic are power by belief, ritual, and the divine, all three of which the Technocrat have, Belief = Paradigm, Ritual = Enlighten Science, Divine = Avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T19:11:01-07:00","id":1540816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540782-have-anyone-done-this?p=1540812#post1540812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that is necessary true, in Chronicle of Darkness Second Sight, Thaumaturge magic are power by belief, ritual, and the divine, all three of which the Technocrat have, Belief = Paradigm, Ritual = Enlighten Science, Divine = Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the reality itself isn't as pliable. Mages from Awakening kind of do the opposite from Ascension: they bring the &quot;true&quot; rules of reality to the Fallen World, even if under their terms.<br /> <br /> There's no reason to think the Technocrats will be able to muster any kind of power, or super science, except maybe by the Thaumaturge rules or similar. Their Avatars mean nothing here.<br /> <br /> IF they do, then they're actually incredibly dangerous to themselves and everyone else, because theirs is the power to bring to reality that they believe, <b>but shouldn't be</b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b, and in the CofD this is the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Assuming they simply keep working as they used to is to ignore the actual metaphysics of the setting. And even if you go ahead, it's preposterous to apply Revised rules when everyone else works through literally another game system.<br /> <br /> Finally, assuming you actually adapts the rules to be compliant with the system, everything else would depend on why would they even give a fuck to this strange world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T19:13:36-07:00","id":1540817,"title":"","content":"You see, the idea of &quot;what would happen if such group ended up in such setting&quot; isn't a bad exercise, or even setup for a chronicle.<br /> <br /> The problem is how you want to break the setting to fully accommodate their powers instead of running with the actual proposal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-20T23:13:13-07:00","id":1540821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540782-have-anyone-done-this?p=1540812#post1540812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that is necessary true, in Chronicle of Darkness Second Sight, Thaumaturge magic are power by belief, ritual, and the divine, all three of which the Technocrat have, Belief = Paradigm, Ritual = Enlighten Science, Divine = Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides any questions about if that really holds true on a metaphysical level - esp. after the changes to the setting in 2e - Thaumaturges don't mess with reality. All of that is just a method for normal humans to access supernatural abilities (that aren't all that special in the CofD).<br /> <br /> So even if you get past the Technocratic paradigm not even applying to the CofD in the first place, the best they can do are some rituals that pale in comparison to full splat capabilities. Given your setup is a Technocratic base, meaning the upper echelons of the Union that understand reality far better than their underlings aren't there to try to reconcile the rigid Technocratic paradigm to a brand new reality where the metaphysical basis of their power doesn't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T00:11:00-07:00","id":1540823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540782-have-anyone-done-this?p=1540821#post1540821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Besides any questions about if that really holds true on a metaphysical level - esp. after the changes to the setting in 2e - Thaumaturges don't mess with reality. All of that is just a method for normal humans to access supernatural abilities (that aren't all that special in the CofD).<br /> <br /> So even if you get past the Technocratic paradigm not even applying to the CofD in the first place, the best they can do are some rituals that pale in comparison to full splat capabilities. Given your setup is a Technocratic base, meaning the upper echelons of the Union that understand reality far better than their underlings aren't there to try to reconcile the rigid Technocratic paradigm to a brand new reality where the metaphysical basis of their power doesn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is still think that belief still kind of effect reality in Chronicle of Darkness, with how the Supernal is affected by Humanity, the Blood Bather ritual never being the same, even when if the ritual was taught by a mentor, the existence of Astral Realm, and other Psychomatic Realm, and the Xenotechnology Endowment from Hunter the Vigil, all evidence that belief does affect reality of Chronicle of Darkness, while it's not as pliable as World of Darkness reality, it's certainly isn't rigid.<br /> <br /> I might not know much about Mage the Ascension metaphysic on how Mage get their power, I know that it have something to do with their Avatar, which is a Spirit type thing, which exist inside of a Mage, that lead them to Enlightment, a thing which Thaumaturge don't have, so I think while they be much more limited in Chronicle of Darkness, a reality that is much less malleable than the one they used to, but they have an actual supernatural spirit living inside of them, so I think they're more powerful than a Thamaturge, but not as powerful as an Awaken Mage. I intend for their power to not metaphysically be compatible with the Chronicle of Darkness reality, they're deviant, one could even say Reality Deviant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T05:19:22-07:00","id":1540828,"title":"","content":"The way the metaphysics works in Chronicles is, whatever you need for your game. It varies and leaves unanswered question specifically because that makes it more flexible, on an out of game basis.<br /> <br /> So, here it is, what works well for the metaphysics of a game about technocrats in the Chronicles setting? Would they still have access to return to the WoD setting? Would they be isolated and join the Seers? Would they become a nameless order and awaken? Would they join the Free Council and try to learn Techn\u00e9?<br /> <br /> How would others react? Would the Arrow see them as a threat? Would the Free Council want to get them to share the sleeper knowledge and culture? Would the Seers see their reality bending as a threat to the Exarchs and try to wipe them out?<br /> <br /> What about others? Without a support network would the become isolate and targets for hunters? Would they be seen as some new kind of Claimed by werewolves and hunted? Would they be experimented on by Deviant's Conspiracies? Would they begin experimenting and create Deviants? Would the God-Machine see them as a problem, destabilising the status quo and send Angels to destroy them? (Or send Angels to con Werewolves/Deviants/hunters into destroying them for it?)<br /> <br /> Would any of the large supernatural corps take an interest? Deva corp? Last Dynasty International?<br /> <br /> Who are they? What type of Technocrats? Are they Void Engineers? New World Order? Interaction X?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T06:10:36-07:00","id":1540829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540782-have-anyone-done-this?p=1540816#post1540816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming they simply keep working as they used to is to ignore the actual metaphysics of the setting. And even if you go ahead, it's preposterous to apply Revised rules when everyone else works through literally another game system.<br /> <br /> Finally, assuming you actually adapts the rules to be compliant with the system, everything else would depend on why would they even give a fuck to this strange world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it fun to mix the rule of Revised into Chronicle of Darkness, it make the character really feel like Reality Deviant.<br /> <br /> Because they need to get back to their reality, or else they would be trap in this strange world, where their power are diminish, and there're strange horror and reality rot everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T06:35:26-07:00","id":1540832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540782-have-anyone-done-this?p=1540828#post1540828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way the metaphysics works in Chronicles is, whatever you need for your game. It varies and leaves unanswered question specifically because that makes it more flexible, on an out of game basis.<br /> <br /> So, here it is, what works well for the metaphysics of a game about technocrats in the Chronicles setting? Would they still have access to return to the WoD setting? Would they be isolated and join the Seers? Would they become a nameless order and awaken? Would they join the Free Council and try to learn Techn\u00e9?<br /> <br /> How would others react? Would the Arrow see them as a threat? Would the Free Council want to get them to share the sleeper knowledge and culture? Would the Seers see their reality bending as a threat to the Exarchs and try to wipe them out?<br /> <br /> What about others? Without a support network would the become isolate and targets for hunters? Would they be seen as some new kind of Claimed by werewolves and hunted? Would they be experimented on by Deviant's Conspiracies? Would they begin experimenting and create Deviants? Would the God-Machine see them as a problem, destabilising the status quo and send Angels to destroy them? (Or send Angels to con Werewolves/Deviants/hunters into destroying them for it?)<br /> <br /> Would any of the large supernatural corps take an interest? Deva corp? Last Dynasty International?<br /> <br /> Who are they? What type of Technocrats? Are they Void Engineers? New World Order? Interaction X?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, the Technocrat would still work like how they did in their World of Darkness Revised Era reality, but their power have been diminish by the virtue of being in a less belief control reality. I don't know why they would join the Seer, they seem like the type of people the typical member of the low ranking technocrat would hate. They can't awaken, because they already have a Avatar inside of them, so they can't channel the Watchtower. And don't the Paradigm kind of act like Techne?<br /> <br /> Why would the Arrow saw them as a threat? They're only a finite amount of them, they're also less power than the average Awaken Mage, and they're limited by their Paradigm unlike the Awaken Mage. What would Free Council learn from the Technocrat that they already don't know? They're from the early 2000s, how much of their knowledge and culture could be important in the year 2020s. I don't think the Seer would notice them, they're only a small handful, even if we counting the Sleeper employee, and the Extraordinary Citizen, that still just a building of people, compare to a whole world.<br /> <br /> Maybe, but that they could hide their magic to be just advance technology. I don't think so, their Avatar seem to be more perfect than a regular Claim. Probably if they somehow get capture by a Deviant Conspiracy. But they would be creating Deviant 100%. The God Machine would probably notice the disturbance in reality, but they aren't really good at dealing with those.<br /> <br /> Most likely, if they can find the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Let's assume this base contain member from all 5 Convention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":".  Accidently post it before finishing it. 08-21-2024, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T06:35:34-07:00","id":1540833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540782-have-anyone-done-this?p=1540823#post1540823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is still think that belief still kind of effect reality in Chronicle of Darkness, with how the Supernal is affected by Humanity, the Blood Bather ritual never being the same, even when if the ritual was taught by a mentor, the existence of Astral Realm, and other Psychomatic Realm, and the Xenotechnology Endowment from Hunter the Vigil, all evidence that belief does affect reality of Chronicle of Darkness, while it's not as pliable as World of Darkness reality, it's certainly isn't rigid.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Certain elements of reality are shaped by human belief&quot; is not the same thing as &quot;if you convince enough people that something is true, it becomes objectively true.&quot;<br /> <br /> Humanity's passive influence on the Supernal is largely in terms of creating new symbolic correspondences. The parts of the Astral Realm that correspond to human culture notably have little direct influence on the material world and/or communicate in human terms because the characters they are communicating with are humans. Even the part of the cosmology where literal figments of human imagination can interact with physically present entities do so at one or two removes or after undergoing transformations that change them to not-insubstantial degree.<br /> <br /> The blood bathing ritual changing from person to person throughout the years is as readily explained by occult variables changing over time (Dreams of Avarice puts forth a mythology in which the literal creator of the universe aims for a world with is constantly changing in opposition to Ammut's drives toward stasis and destruction). Ditto for Xenotechnology gizmos, which need &quot;aliens cores&quot; and tissue samples from monsters and facilities \u2014 the need for constant maintenance is as significant as the diversity of takes on the same schematic.<br /> <br /> In Chronicles, the human soul is capable of influencing the world through magical processes, which Mummy and Mage's crossover material implies is because the world and the human soul are made from the same building blocks. These processes exist independently of human belief \u2014 the God-Machine essentially performs miracles at an industrial scale by leveraging symbolism most people will never see, High Speech messages can be found in the world with no human origin, and assorted other magical effects can appear spontaneously with a pre-existing connection to human culture that's tenuous at best.<br /> <br /> The biggest non-localized changes in setting metaphysics on the books are either the product of attempts at Ascension or the consequences of a major interaction with a godlike being (e.g. the Sundering, the change from Oracles to Heroes, etc.). Deviant presents a framework in which setting-altering consequences can arise from the Projects of conspiracies, but that's a double-whammy of active human efforts and meddling with forces beyond their full comprehension. Belief affects reality in Chronicles the way human occupation affects an environment \u2014 deforestation might happen to the woods at the edge of town, but it happens because people with axes went and chopped down trees for building materials, not because they thought the boundary between the parts of the land with trees and log cabins was closer to the river.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T06:44:36-07:00","id":1540834,"title":"","content":"Thank for that lore bit, but can you explain how Thaumaturge magic is power by belief, ritual, and the divine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T07:41:07-07:00","id":1540838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540782-have-anyone-done-this?p=1540834#post1540834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank for that lore bit, but can you explain how Thaumaturge magic is power by belief, ritual, and the divine?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is how it is defined in the Second Sight book, and subsequent supplements have used this as the default.<br /> <br /> There is no large metaphysical explanation in-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T07:58:02-07:00","id":1540839,"title":"","content":"Since there is no Consensus in CofD, perhaps you could treat them like Proiximi. The Curse is tied to helping the Avatar maintain their paradigm's occult stability, the Severe effect is what happens when its destabilized and the Persistent curse is thematically tied to their foci.<br /> <br /> It might also be interesting to throw in something akin to an occult allergic reaction to the Abyss, since their Avatar has no clue what it is or how to deal with its type of reality warping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T18:39:30-07:00","id":1540869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540782-have-anyone-done-this?p=1540829#post1540829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because they need to get back to their reality, or else they would be trap in this strange world, where their power are diminish, and there're strange horror and reality rot everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is a single base, and their sole focus for now is to go back to their reality, then their interaction with other actors of the supernatural society will mostly depend on local representatives and politics, which is anyone's guess.<br /> <br /> As they're in another realm, most of the Union's usual takes have no reason to happen. This world is as it is, monsters aren't Reality Deviants here, magic doesn't disrupt this reality either, there is no Consensus to preserve even if they cared. They would have to learn a lot before even being able to learn about dangers like the Abyss, which is a far, far worse form of Paradox for reality at large than what they're used to.<br /> <br /> They have no previous reason to be enemies or friends of any faction until help or hindrance to their goals factor in, and there will be a huge difference between their stance as they try to go home from when they give up and decide to settle.<br /> <br /> What will be more of a shock, though, is general stance about secrets. WoD is a setting thoroughly defined by stark paranoia and complete secrecy. CofD is far more of a Do What You Will place, with more nuanced interactions and no Veil as the Union understands it. That attitude, more than even their powers, will stand out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T18:43:51-07:00","id":1541048,"title":"","content":"It never came in our game as we had no dealings with the old setting and just dove in with new setting from COD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}